  "claim": "Wisconsin was the state in which John Flammang Schrank from New York attempted to assassinate Republican president Theodore Roosevelt in October 1912 and again in November 1916.",
  "evidencia": "Page: John Flammang Schrank. Sentence: John Flammang Schrank (March 5, 1876 – September 15, 1943) was a resident of New York, best known for his attempt to assassinate former U.S. President Theodore Roosevelt on October 14, 1912, in Milwaukee, Wisconsin.\nPage: Theodore Roosevelt. Sentence: Theodore Roosevelt Jr. ( ; October 27, 1858 – January 6, 1919) was an American statesman, author, explorer, soldier, naturalist, and reformer who served as the 26th President of the United States from 1901 to 1909.\nPage: Theodore Roosevelt. Sentence: As a leader of the Republican Party during this time, he became a driving force for the Progressive Era in the United States in the early 20th century.",
